## kill all docker containers

```bash
docker stop $(docker ps -q)
```

## get into docker container

```bash
docker ps
docker exec -it CONTAINER_ID bash
```


Port mapping -p port-outside:port-inside
Volume mapping -v ext-vol:inside-vol
docker inspect [container name/id]
docker logs [container name/id]

## create volume to store data written by the container

```bash
docker create volume data_volume
```

## volume mounting

```bash
docker run -v data_volume:/var/lib/mysql mysql (creates volume automatically if it doesnt exist yet)
```

## bind mounting

```bash
docker run -v /some/path:/var/lib/mysql mysql (pass an existing dir)
```

```bash
docker run --mount \
type=bind,source=/some/path,target=/var/lib/mysql mysql
```

## show all volumes

```bash
ls /var/lib/docker/volumes
```

## docker-compose.yml

```
main_image:
  subimage1:
    image: my_img
    ports:
      - 1000:80
  subimage2:
    image: my_another_image (repo)
    ports:
      - 1001:80
    links: 
      - subimage1
   my_subimage:
     build: ./my_subimage (Dockerfile path)
     links:
      - subimage1
      - subimage2
```

## versions
- Version 1 forces using links
- Version 2 and higher enables no use of links, must begin from 'version: 2\nservices:', introduces depends_on feature to enforce startup order
- Version 3 which supports docker swarm feature
